xfs_quota -x -c 'report -h' /data
🧠 7️⃣ Step 5: Verify Quotas
xfs_quota -x -c 'report -h' /data
Example output:
Project       Used    Soft    Hard
project1      2G      8G      10G

1️⃣ Check Quota Status
xfs_quota -x -c 'report -h' /mountpoint
-x → expert mode (required for setting limits)
-c 'command' → run a command
report -h → human-readable quota report
Example:
xfs_quota -x -c 'report -h' /data
🧠 2️⃣ Set User Quota
xfs_quota -x -c 'limit bsoft=<soft limit> bhard=<hard limit> <username>' /mountpoint
bsoft → soft block limit (disk space)
bhard → hard block limit
<username> → user name
Example:
xfs_quota -x -c 'limit bsoft=100m bhard=120m user1' /data
🧠 3️⃣ Set Group Quota
xfs_quota -x -c 'limit bsoft=<soft limit> bhard=<hard limit> <groupname>' /mountpoint
Example:
xfs_quota -x -c 'limit bsoft=500m bhard=600m devteam' /data
